# Sandbox Control runtime gates. build-and-push.yml applies the Connector
# Authority root (KMS keys, control tables, the OTP pepper, the Hub) unattended
# on every qualifying main push, which deliberately removed the human
# plan-review gate. Merging a change to the gate file IS the apply — it is on
# on.push.paths, so the next push mutates live sandbox to match it — which
# makes this file the one remaining human control point, and the natural
# replacement for the review gate that was given up.
#
# The reader is owned alongside it because it is what decides whether a gate
# file is valid at all: weaken its validation and a shape the guard would have
# refused reaches Terraform. The fence and its fixtures are owned for the same
# reason one step out: C5 (the shared writer lock), C6 (the gate-reader capture
# form) and C7 (the fully-dark teardown refusal) are what keep the deploy leg's
# safety logic from being edited away, and build-and-push.yml itself is too
# broad to own.
#
# NOTE, so this is not mistaken for more than it is: as of 2026-08-09 main's
# branch protection has require_code_owner_reviews=false and
# enforce_admins=false, so these entries REQUEST review, they do not require it.
# Making this a real gate is a branch-protection change, not a CODEOWNERS one.
# See the prod-rollout ledger entry for that open decision.
/.github/control-sandbox-runtime-gates.json         justin@layerv.ai
/.github/scripts/control-sandbox-runtime-gates.py   justin@layerv.ai
/scripts/check-control-leg-surfaced.sh              justin@layerv.ai
/tests/scripts/check-control-leg-surfaced_test.sh   justin@layerv.ai
